<title>USA: Kennecott Utah smelter back on stream.</title>
<headline>Kennecott Utah smelter back on stream.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kennecott Utah Copper Corp's smelter is back on stream and will reach full capacity later in the year, company spokesman Louie Cononelos said.</p>
<p>&quot;The smelter has started,&quot; Cononelos said. &quot;Everything is ramping up as planned.&quot; The smelter began operating Tuesday.</p>
<p>The 310,000 short tons per year smelter was shut April 15 for 42 days of maintenance to iron out glitches which have plagued the new plant since its commissioning.</p>
<p>&quot;We plan to be at full capacity later in the year,&quot; Cononelos said.</p>
<p>((Huw Jones, New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
